And it was Mobutu's personal response to the European suit and tie. Well, it was his personal response that he more or less copied directly from China. It had what was then called a Mao color, but to make it a bit different, the color was slightly elongated with the scarf in the place of a tie. And voila, the Abacost. As part of Authenticité, Mobutu had come up with a new national dress code, and he made the Abacost the official office uniform in Zaire.
这是蒙博托对欧洲西装和领带的个人回应。好吧，这是他个人回应，他或多或少直接从中国抄袭了它。它有当时所谓的“毛领”，但为了让它有点不同，领子稍微拉长了，用围巾代替了领带。瞧，阿巴科斯特。作为“真实性”的一部分，蒙博托制定了新的国家着装规范，并使阿巴科斯特成为扎伊尔的官方办公室制服。

